From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: Do not keep the J72 peripheral session over s2idle

The iPad Air J72 wakes on a PMIC event when its Lightning source is removed
during s2idle.  A peripheral session kept across that sleep no longer
describes the physical connection after this event.  Continuing it produced
USB protocol errors when the cable was restored and left the gadget
unreachable.

Use DWC2's ordinary disconnect and reset path on J72.  This recovered the
gadget cleanly after a sleep-time cable cycle, while an unchanged-source
control retained its qualified charging grant across sleep.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -313,6 +313,13 @@ static void dwc2_set_apple_silicon_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	 * for power-off and restart, never for sleep.
 	 */
 	p->s2idle_keep_session = true;
+	/*
+	 * J72 wakes when its Lightning source disappears.  The session is no
+	 * longer valid then, so use the normal disconnect and reset path.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j72"))
+		p->s2idle_keep_session = false;
+
 	p->g_rx_fifo_size = 539;
 	p->host_nperio_tx_fifo_size = 16;
 	p->g_np_tx_fifo_size = 16;
-- 
